# 04 — Stop criteria

<!-- GEN: Why: knowing when not to simplify protects behavior and approved decisions as much as the techniques do. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rule S12 with the workspace's gate names and decision notation. -->

Stop simplifying when:

| Situation | Do instead |
|---|---|
| Behavior or a public contract would change | Return to {{gate_for_changes}} |
| A workspace decision ({{decision_notation}}) requires the abstraction | Leave it; mention it in the report if it looks unnecessary |
| The gain is cosmetic (renaming taste, reordering) | Leave it |
| A hot path would change without measurement | Measure first or leave it |
| The next step needs code outside the diff | Record a separate task |
| Checks turn red and the cause is not obvious | Revert the last step |

